{"answer":"The rotating community committee will be made up of fishers who are elected each month by a simple majority of those present at the monthly gathering. Each fisher gets one vote. The committee meets quarterly to review the violation logs and can issue a written notice of a temporary ban to any fisher who has had three or more infractions within a 12‑month period. The lake steward is the one who actually enforces the ban by denying access to fishing gear or the shared fishing grounds until the next season. The committee’s decision is final unless a majority of the community votes to overturn it within one month, at which point the steward will reverse the ban. This gives the committee a clear, democratic method of selection and a concrete enforcement mechanism through the steward’s authority over gear and access.

